Volume 03, Batch 0001 — Chapters 101–110 — complete.

Ten chapters delivered in `chapters/volume-03/`, close third person on Marek Venn, no viewpoint shift
anywhere in the batch. This is the first prose batch of Volume 03 and it opens the volume on the
delivered canon and not on the series outline's fragile charter: the charter is strong and has a hole
(clause four binds one office), nobody hostile has ever been in this building, the committed central
pressure is kept exactly as written, and the crew's maintenance obligation is discharged, so the
volume opens with five people drifting outward and a man discovering he is not needed.

The batch: the school corner's floor is wet and the water is the boundary's own drinking water, traced
to a stone taken out of a course and put back in lime; three candidate rooms are refused in the right
hands and the boundary ends a day with no room; nine children cross a fill that has moved three times
and stay on the far side; the school corner is then shut as a room — a correct, cheap closure that
closes no corridor on any day of the week and strands nobody; a competent Stonelight Compact inspector
arrives on a lawful permit that the charter does not cover, the boundary writes a four-sentence
procedure for a body it never wrote one for, and the plan's third column leaves the building in a
clerk's hand; the elected keeper goes up four days of road to keep a promise; the boundary runs the
rest of the batch without him and finds that it runs perfectly well; a second sheet names a fourth
object of care; nine register boxes cross the waist and one of the three open days is lost against a
closure added; a competent guild office closes a water-lock with four households behind it and the
first toll on a closed door is a form; and the plan's first column is read aloud and the boundary finds
out it has been writing down a nine-hundred-year-old permission instead of a population.

Refused, deliberately: the Marker stage, which is owed at Chapter 112 and is refused out loud in
Chapter 109 with the clerk entering that she did not understand the second half of it; the keeper's
promise, which is Batch 0002's scene in the twenty-second week; and the road and the counter, so there
is no viewpoint shift.

A partial checkpoint draft of Chapters 101–108 existed in this batch directory and was replaced in
full rather than continued, because a batch is one voice, one set of numbers and one calendar and the
replacement was reviewed as a whole. The fact is recorded in `state/continuity.md`.

An independent review was run in the writing session. Its findings were repaired in the chapters and in
the state files, not deferred: the boundary's hours now add to thirty-six and the figure is a hundred
and fifty-three and a quarter; Chapter 110 is dated to the fifth day of its week; the keeper of the
plan is a man and not a woman; the Chapter 110 finding no longer contradicts itself; the clerk no
longer claims to have written the plan's first column; the four-sentence procedure is argued in four
hands and is misread in the reading, and the misreading is the point; the low end's water mechanism is
the canon's six minutes and not three bells; two internal miscounts, one wrong week reference, one
wrong unit of count and two forward references are corrected; two narration slips that staged Nera
Oduya leaving are cut; Marek Venn no longer announces and resolves his own departure; the review page's
blank has one owner and not two; the keeper's ring is refused out loud instead of used; twelve pieces
of meta language and one 143-character repeated clause are cut; the two required missing beats — the
Marker refusal and Nera Oduya being asked for a piece of work — are both supplied; Wen Pask is named
in his own action; and every bold span in the batch is closed inside the paragraph that opens it.

`reviews/volume-03/batch-0001.md` does not exist as a file and is still owed to the reviewer's phase,
as are `reviews/volume-02/batch-0003.md`, `batch-0004.md` and `batch-0005.md`. `state/continuity.md`
is the record of this batch's review and repairs.

State files updated. Next phase: `workspace/volume-03/batch-0002/PROMPT.md`, Chapters 111–120, the
twenty-second and twenty-third weeks.
